        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castlebay, Barra, Outer Hebrides, Scotland\n- Products: Kisimul Castle\n- Concepts: Scottish Gaelic names\n\nFacts:\n- Castlebay is the main village and a community council area on the island of Barra in the Outer Hebrides, Scotland.\n- Castlebay has the Scottish Gaelic name \"Bàgh a' Chaisteil.\"\n- Kisimul Castle is also known as Kiessimul Castle.\n- Kisimul Castle is a small medieval castle on a small island off Castlebay, Barra, in the Outer Hebrides, Scotland.\n- Kisimul Castle has the Scottish Gaelic name \"Caisteal Chiosmuil.\"",
